{"id":"translator-and-historical-edition-notes-part-8","label":"Translator and historical edition notes (part 8)","headingNoteRefs":"","context":"","kind":"commentary","blocks":[{"text":"[^n2988]: Matt. xxv. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2988"},{"text":"[^n2989]: Lit. table (cf. Peshitta).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2989"},{"text":"[^n2990]: Matt. xxv. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2990"},{"text":"[^n2991]: Matt. xxv. 29.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2991"},{"text":"[^n2992]: Matt. xxv. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2992"},{"text":"[^n2993]: Luke xii. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2993"},{"text":"[^n2994]: Luke xii. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2994"},{"text":"[^n2995]: Luke xii. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2995"},{"text":"[^n2996]: cf. Peshitta (and Greek).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2996"},{"text":"[^n2997]: Luke xii. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2997"},{"text":"[^n2998]: Matt. xxv. 31.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2998"},{"text":"[^n2999]: Matt. xxv. 32.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n2999"},{"text":"[^n3000]: Matt. xxv. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3000"},{"text":"[^n3001]: Or, and setteth; but the Peshitta confirms the rendering given above.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3001"},{"text":"[^n3002]: Matt. xxv. 34.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3002"},{"text":"[^n3003]: cf. § 17, 17, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3003"},{"text":"[^n3004]: Matt. xxv. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3004"},{"text":"[^n3005]: Matt. xxv. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3005"},{"text":"[^n3006]: Matt. xxv. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3006"},{"text":"[^n3007]: Matt. xxv. 38.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3007"},{"text":"[^n3008]: Matt. xxv. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3008"},{"text":"[^n3009]: Matt. xxv. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3009"},{"text":"[^n3010]: Perfect tenses, as in Peshitta.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3010"},{"text":"[^n3011]: Matt. xxv. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3011"},{"text":"[^n3012]: Matt. xxv. 42.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3012"},{"text":"[^n3013]: Matt. xxv. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3013"},{"text":"[^n3014]: Matt. xxv. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3014"},{"text":"[^n3015]: Matt. xxv. 45.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3015"},{"text":"[^n3016]: Matt. xxv. 46.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3016"},{"text":"[^n3017]: Matt. xxvi. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3017"},{"text":"[^n3018]: Borg. ms., the Lord Jesus.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3018"},{"text":"[^n3019]: Matt. xxvi. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3019"},{"text":"[^n3020]: Matt. xxvi. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3020"},{"text":"[^n3021]: Matt. xxvi. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3021"},{"text":"[^n3022]: Matt. xxvi. 5.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3022"},{"text":"[^n3023]: Luke xxii. 2b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3023"},{"text":"[^n3024]: Luke xxii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3024"},{"text":"[^n3025]: Luke xxii. 4a; Matt. xxvi. 15a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3025"},{"text":"[^n3026]: Mark xiv. 11a; Matt. xxvi. 15b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3026"},{"text":"[^n3027]: Probably the letter that stands for and should be repeated, and the phrase rendered and appointed.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3027"},{"text":"[^n3028]: So Vat. ms. (following Peshitta) and Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary. Borg. ms., followed by Ciasca, has dirhams of money.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3028"},{"text":"[^n3029]: Luke xxii. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3029"},{"text":"[^n3030]: Lit. became responsible unto. Syriac versions as in text above (cf. § 44, 33).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3030"},{"text":"[^n3031]: The Arabic (lit. a stumbling or a cause of stumbling) doubtless represents the Syriac.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3031"},{"text":"[^n3032]: Mark xiv. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3032"},{"text":"[^n3033]: John xiii. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3033"},{"text":"[^n3034]: John xiii. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3034"},{"text":"[^n3035]: John xiii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3035"},{"text":"[^n3036]: John xiii. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3036"},{"text":"[^n3037]: John xiii. 5.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3037"},{"text":"[^n3038]: John xiii. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3038"},{"text":"[^n3039]: John xiii. 7.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3039"},{"text":"[^n3040]: John xiii. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3040"},{"text":"[^n3041]: John xiii. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3041"},{"text":"[^n3042]: John xiii. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3042"},{"text":"[^n3043]: The Arabic word means swimmeth. The Syriac versions have is bathed, which Borg. ms. misreads bathed, and Vat. ms. (followed by Ciasca) corrupts into batheth, rendering it swimmeth.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3043"},{"text":"[^n3044]: John xiii. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3044"},{"text":"[^n3045]: John xiii. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3045"},{"text":"[^n3046]: John xiii. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3046"},{"text":"[^n3047]: John xiii. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3047"},{"text":"[^n3048]: John xiii. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3048"},{"text":"[^n3049]: John xiii. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3049"},{"text":"[^n3050]: John xiii. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3050"},{"text":"[^n3051]: John xiii. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3051"},{"text":"[^n3052]: Or, This my saying.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3052"},{"text":"[^n3053]: John xiii. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3053"},{"text":"[^n3054]: John xiii. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3054"},{"text":"[^n3055]: Luke xxii. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3055"},{"text":"[^n3056]: Luke xxii. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3056"},{"text":"[^n3057]: Luke xxii. 29.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3057"},{"text":"[^n3058]: Luke xxii. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3058"},{"text":"[^n305